  "sharedContext": {
    "summary": "Replace visually strange production work keys with a recognisable keyring on the desk; Codex candidate had identity but was tiny/hard to recognise at actual size (brief M0, relayed, not owner verbatim).",
    "missingContext": [
      "owner low-angle photos and perspective drawing in QP Orch not available",
      "M1 reference images are third-party stock photos/pen sketch, not copied",
      "unknown how owner viewed each version"
    ]
  },
  "ownerMessages": [
    {
      "id": "M1",
      "locator": "user message mid-turn after the handoff brief",
      "verbatim": "Some additional reference images I got by searching, that may help: they didn't produce good Codex results but you are better at drawing.",
      "kind": "reference supplied"
    },
    {
      "id": "M2",
      "after": "v1",
      "verbatim": "Make the ring smaller and place it through the keyholes, or arrange the keys so the keyholes are hidden."
    },
    {
      "id": "M3",
      "after": "v2",
      "verbatim": "Smaller is good, but the ring still reads wrong.  Place the box-shaped object in front of the holes in the keys and the ring behind all of them, so that it is plausible that the ring goes through the holes in the keys without having to figure out how to draw that."
    },
    {
      "id": "M4",
      "after": "v3",
      "verbatim": "Improvement, still not there.  How about we move the ring to just a small portion visible, as in the attached (rough) red area of the screenshot?",
      "attachment": "images/owner-red-annotated-screenshot-of-v3.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "M5",
      "after": "v4",
      "verbatim": "Much better.  Test the scene composition using localhost:5173, that's open and no other agents are working."
    },
    {
      "id": "M6",
      "after": "v5-accepted (art and proposed placement, limits disclosed)",
      "verbatim": "Accept for swap"
    }
  ],
